        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_9317ed520d65469dad4ecfbf8a8a7337",
      "statement": "Which user-document properties appear in JWTs is the account-properties-claims list on the always-on auth feature. This repo's setup reads and writes that list through admin.getFeatureConfig and admin.updateFeatureConfig for feature auth — it does not use an /auth-config/{srvId} endpoint. ulabase.setup.consents.ts merges in latestConsents/tos and latestConsents/pp because the guards rule compares those values on the token rather than reading the database; a missing claim compares false and blocks every token-authenticated user permanently.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://ulabase.setup.consents.ts#L163-L163",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4bb93358150cc115e30752b7ebea212679a6225d930d21c0222f812c6f849702:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://ulabase.setup.consents.ts#L251-L278",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9da31f401dee8336daecb0123438b43cc6039b4debbf3ebf9747986f90f42491:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_30cd17b589aa4d6dbd27a0d5fff2c5ca",
      "statement": "Guards are server-side rules that block requests based on conditions. The consents gate uses a guard rule that blocks authenticated users who haven't accepted current Terms/Privacy Policy, returns HTTP 451, excludes anonymous callers/auth endpoints/acceptance request, and importantly does not exclude /users/me to make the gate work without client-side probing.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/consents-signal.ts#L8-L15",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:07638b19f7240f900f536067815181f6a57b12d76cabbe3c9fd3e7e6a48cc582:"
        },
        {
