    },
    {
      "id": "claim_f77f78c79f1e48a89e0ea3c0f7a60c14",
      "statement": "The consents user schema requires only _id and roles; password, profile, latestConsents, consents, socialAuths, teams, and team are optional so that registrations and invitations which insert incomplete documents still validate. acceptedAt is typed as a BSON date via _$date inside the stored schema, and _id is required even on a PUT /users/{id} where it arrives in the path rather than the body.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://ulabase.setup.consents.ts#L65-L117",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b3ac9478443fd818f5bbb8cbca4a0d90681450fadc21388eec769df1456416c3:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_bb86053c616e4ae1be67175a398733ea",
      "statement": "userCanPatchOwnConsents is the only authorization for PATCH /users/{userId} of consents: it is scoped to the caller's own user id and to the consents field via bson-request-whitelist, and its mergeRequest stamps latestConsents with the current TOS_VERSION/PP_VERSION and $pushes the same entry onto the consents history server-side. The client states no versions or timestamps; without this permission the acceptance is a 403 and the guards rule never sees the request.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://ulabase.setup.consents.ts#L220-L248",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d691885900551d601f5fe1163ab4cf3a3794f941d8ea4050d1ed2ae1e06c83e4:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://ulabase.setup.consents.ts#L62-L63",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e6899fd99fe7801acde1ee820245e03ee978b96e284e6b1dc7479c6b2ebf6786:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_ec348044b9fd40d7b50d43049a82e60a",
      "statement": "The consentsGate guards rule blocks when either the ToS or the Privacy Policy acceptance is missing, compares the full derived condition so a TOS_VERSION/PP_VERSION bump is reported as outstanding work, returns status_code 451, and sets on_error to allow so a rule that cannot be evaluated cannot lock every user out.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://ulabase.setup.consents.ts#L119-L161",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8143dba70bb12cfe0653808865cd5ee1c3e44a20c90ecbf7422957cb518dab0c:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://ulabase.setup.consents.ts#L285-L313",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9a26db9fa9079d7b8ed9497a318fe1bc8ee5e13a91845159263843a88445893f:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_827aaf2d65064338b3850ed3883d7c0f",
      "statement": "TOS_VERSION and PP_VERSION at the top of ulabase.setup.consents.ts are the only place the demanded legal-document versions live: both the acceptance permission's mergeRequest and the guard condition derive from them, so publishing new terms is editing two strings and re-running setup. The Version line in public/terms.html and public/privacy.html remains the one place kept in step by hand.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://NOTES.md#L208-L212",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e8db9024c93ed9dd2e13709908b23726161163ebdbd06e3e1d659f6a9e15811d:"
